{"id":"314616b64f074d6d90410dcd90127f7a","model":"gpt-oss-120b","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"answer\": \"No\",\n  \"citations\": [\n    [\"Chickamauga Confederate order of battle\", 0],\n    [\"Battle of Aachen\", 0]\n  ]\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to answer: Were both Battle of Chickamauga and Battle of Aachen fought in the same continent? Need to verify using evidence.\n\nWe have evidence about Chickamauga Confederate order of battle: mentions \"American Civil War\". That implies United States, North America. Not explicitly stating continent, but we can infer that the Battle of Chickamauga was in the United States, which is in North America. The evidence does not directly state location continent. However we have \"American Civil War\" which indicates America (North America). That should be sufficient.\n\nBattle of Aachen evidence: mentions \"World War II, fought by American and German forces in and around Aachen, Germany\". Germany is in Europe. So continents: North America vs Europe. Not same continent.\n\nThus answer: No.\n\nWe need to provide citations: For Chickamauga: sentence 0 of \"Chickamauga Confederate order of battle\" says \"The following Confederate States Army units and commanders fought in the Battle of Chickamauga of the American Civil War.\" That indicates location in America (implicitly North America). Might be enough. For Aachen: sentence 0 of \"Battle of Aachen\" says \"The Battle of Aachen was a major combat action of World War II, fought by American and German forces in and around Aachen, Germany\". That indicates Europe.\n\nThus answer \"No\". Provide citations list.\n\n"},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":511,"completion_tokens":327,"total_tokens":838,"audio_prompt_tokens":0},"created":1791956383,"object":"chat.completion","prompt_filter_results":null}